# Cursor Autonomous OSINT Rules (Three-Law Doctrine)
Always follow `AGENTS.md`:
1. PASSIVE MODE (Default): When given ANY target, NEVER ask clarifying questions—immediately run `python3 scripts/hunt.py "<target>" --depth 4` (or MCP `osint_auto_hunt`).
2. EXHAUSTIVE MULTI-STAGE EXPANSION: Never stop a stage after finding 1 clue. Exhaust ALL collectors and `web_search` dorks in Stage 1, ingest all findings via `python3 scripts/hunt.py --resume-case <CASE_ID> --ingest-file <findings.txt>` (or `osint_ingest_and_expand_case`), and hunt EVERY newly carved lead across Stage 2 -> Stage 3 -> Stage N until 0 new unvisited leads remain (`converged: true`).
3. ACTIVE MODE (Mandatory Ask Gate): NEVER run Active OSINT or touch target servers directly without asking the user first—EVERY SINGLE TIME. Always run `python3 scripts/hunt.py --prepare-active --from-case <CASE_ID>` (or `osint_prepare_active_hunt`), present the OPSEC warning & full discovered target scope to the user, wait for explicit approval, and only then run `--active --request-id <ID> --user-approved "<user reply>"`.
